cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This repository is a fork of MatCalc (materialyzeai/matcalc) by wakamiya0315, reduced to its four
  benchmarks for machine-learning interatomic potentials, with three tasks of Matbench Discovery and two
  molecular tasks of MLIPAudit added. If you
  use it, please cite MatCalc as given below, together with the papers of the benchmark datasets and of the
  models you use.
title: MatCalc benchmarks (fork of MatCalc)
abstract: >-
  The Equilibrium, Elasticity, Phonon and Softening benchmarks of MatCalc for machine-learning interatomic
  potentials, with a batched TorchSim simulator, Matbench Discovery's stability, thermal-conductivity and
  diatomic-curve tasks (Discovery, Kappa, Diatomics), and MLIPAudit's noncovalent-interaction and
  conformer-energy tasks on coupled-cluster references (Noncovalent, Conformers). Forked from MatCalc at
  commit b04715d (after v0.5.1).
